NFG 1 R "Kohlberg and Mertens (1986), Section 2.8 (game Delta)" { "I" "II" }

{ { "T" "M" "B" }
{ "L" "R" }
}
"A zero-sum game used to show that the requirement of sequentiality in every equivalent tree may be impossible to satisfy: every tree with this reduced normal form (such as the trees of Figures 7 and 10) must have a sequential equilibrium, but the unique sequential equilibria of different trees differ. Its Nash equilibria form a single connected component; the paper's stable set contains the equilibria (T,(1/4,3/4)) and (T,(3/4,1/4)).

The paper calls this game :math:`\Delta`. Player I's strategies are T, M and B; player II's are L and R."

